   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to owner liability\nfor failure of operator to comply with certain posted maximum speed limits in\nthe town of Yorktown, Westchester county; and to amend the general municipal\nlaw, in relation to making technical corrections",
    "basePrintNo": "S7802",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7802-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1180-e, V & T L; amd §371-a, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7802\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to owner\nliability for failure of operator to comply with certain posted maximum\nspeed limits in the town of Yorktown, Westchester county; and to amend\nthe general municipal law, in relation to making technical corrections\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAllows Yorktown to install temporary speed cameras in work zones.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:.\n\nMakes the necessary changes to the vehicle and traffic law as added by\nchapter 421 of the laws of 2021 in order to expand the existing highway\nwork zone speed camera program to all municipal roadways within the town\nof Yorktown, Westchester County.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOur road work zones are dangerous areas for those working to repair the\nroads. Too often, people speed through these areas placing road workers\nin grave danger.  It is impossible to station a police officer in every\nwork zone across the state. Therefore, it is imperative that we allow\nmunicipalities to install temporary speed cameras in these areas in\norder to discourage dangerous driving habits so that we may better\nprotect our road workers.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-24: A.9283A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis revenues generated through this legislation will offset the cost to\nlocal government of installing and maintaining the cameras.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nNinety days after it shall have become law\n",
